-- --opens specification (seg/WRITING.md, rule 6) for CrossTerm (doc/cross-term.pdf,
-- Sections 3 (end) to 5: Corollary 7 (s'), Lemmas 8, 9, 11, 13, 14, Theorems 10,
-- 15, Definition 12): one entry per declaration, generated from --opened
-- (28 Oct 2026) and checked against the note by kind.  Kinds as in double.opens,
-- h4.opens and cup.opens; in addition:
--   types and levels: PtMap, PtSec, PtEquiv, Maps.PMO, PiOne.O, isEquiv, isSet,
--     HC, isConn, Over.C; the numerals two, three, four, five, plus and the
--     library aliases KZ2, KZ4, kz2, kz4, Zab, KK.K, KK.pt;
--   by-definition steps of the text: Induced.L, PiOne.comp (LMult.L-def,
--     comp-def); ptcomp, ptconst, ptid; KMap.conj (loop-k22: conj_1 is
--     e_1 ; - ; e_1^-1), Lev.conj, Lev.eBi (f-sq); EDef.phi, EDef.E, ENat.E,
--     ENat.E', ENat.lG, ENat.Gs, ENat.M, ENat.M', BilAt.M', BilAt.Theta, Lev.jB,
--     pt-comp, Acc.fun (Theta c x = j_B (E c x)); CupSquare.e1inv,
--     PtMapLoops.pt0, r (LO.pt0 is the target point r of ev), ev, ev-pt, R and
--     FT.tr (ev P is FT.tr pt0 P, the form ev-ap is stated in); kbar, kappa,
--     the parts of c'' (N-def); Cross.f, CrossGen.Dp, Dhat, tau, Cj, Cj-fun, delta, and
--     Maps.D (diag-null: D_p q = (f p)^-1 . f (p . q)); pt-inv, Acc.inv
--     (e_2^-1 is the section of e_2: cell-of, f-sq); Diag.diag, Diag.dprime,
--     Diag.M, m0, DiagAt.M, m0, ClassesAt.cls, ClassesAt.f0, Defect.f0, hcl,
--     STr.inc (cross: cls (dprime c) is [diag c]); k21 (in loop-k22 and k21-sq,
--     before its lock); tau-fun, tau-inv (tau-def, tau-inv-def, before their
--     lock); Doubling.sq, Dbl.Stmt; trans (trans p refl is p);
--   K(Z,1) of the circle (EM1.K1 -> TrivG.K -> img, Zab, EMSpace.K, KK.K) is
--     identified with KK.K 1 in k21, loop-k22 and k21-sq only (as in
--     CupSquare.e1), k21 being locked afterwards;
--   extras, not steps of the text:
--     K(Z,2) as a type (KZ2 -> KK.K two -> EMSpace.K -> EMn.Kstage -> stage2 ->
--       EM2.K2 -> Deloop.Torsors.Tor) in the entries binding x : KZ2 (ETwo.e-two,
--       e-zero, Kill.e-c'', theta-pt, N-def, N, N-lev, CrossGen.delta-def, parts-def,
--       diag-null): the etaV defect of doc/etav-lock-diagnostic.txt, as in h4.opens;
--     Kill.e-c'' opens subst, FT.tr and PtMapLoops.ev, as BilAt.key-pt does;
--     Cross.cross opens Quotient.Quot.image / Quot.inc when comparing hcl with
--       ClassesAt.cls (checker strategy).
-- Check: segd All.seg --opens cross.opens ; every line "nothing else opened".
